```tsx
// PersonHero uses more top padding to clear navbar
<div className="px-4 md:px-8 lg:px-12 pt-16 md:pt-20 pb-8 md:pb-12">
```

## PersonFilmography Pattern

Filmography uses `MediaCard` in `MediaScroller` for visual consistency and respects card display preference:

```tsx
import { PersonFilmography } from "@/components/features/person";

<PersonFilmography person={person} className="mt-8" />
```

Features:
- **Tabs**: Movies / TV Shows with counts
- **Filter tabs**: All / Cast / Crew (inline toggle, not dropdown) - defaults to "All"
- **Role display**: Shows character name (cast) or job (crew) as subtitle on each card
- **Browse All link**: Links to `/browse` with cast/crew filter for the person
- **Grouped by decade**: 2020s, 2010s, 2000s, etc.
- **Uses MediaCard**: Respects user's poster/wide card preference
- **Talk show filtering**: Excludes news/talk show appearances
- **No truncation**: Shows all credits (with posters or backdrops depending on mode)

```tsx
// Decade scrollers structure - uses MediaCard with both sizing classes
const posterCardClass = "w-[130px] sm:w-[145px] md:w-[160px] flex-shrink-0";
const wideCardClass = "w-[220px] sm:w-[260px] md:w-[300px] flex-shrink-0";

<MediaScroller title="2020s">
  {credits.map((credit) => (
    <MediaCard
      item={creditToListItem(credit)}
      className={posterCardClass}
      wideClassName={wideCardClass}
      showRating
      subtitle={credit.character || credit.job}  // Shows role/job below title
    />
  ))}
</MediaScroller>
```

## UpcomingLatestSection Component

Shows recent and upcoming projects in a single scroller:

```tsx
import { UpcomingLatestSection } from "@/components/features/person";

<UpcomingLatestSection
  castCredits={person.combined_credits.cast || []}
  crewCredits={person.combined_credits.crew || []}
  className="mt-8"
/>
```

**Features:**
- Combines last 5 releases + all upcoming in one scroller
- Order: Latest (most recent first) → Upcoming (soonest first)
- Shows character/job + release date as subtitle
- Upcoming items show relative time ("In 3 days", "In 2 months")
- Ratings hidden for upcoming (may not exist yet)
- Filters out talk shows automatically
- Only renders if there are items to show

**Date range:**
- "Latest": Released within last 24 months (`LATEST_MONTHS` constant)
- "Upcoming": Release date in the future

## PersonCard for Cast Sections

Use `PersonCard` in cast carousels for linking to person pages:

```tsx
import { PersonCard } from "@/components/features/person";

// In cast scrollers
{cast.map((member) => (
  <PersonCard
    key={member.id}
    person={member}
    size="md" // or "sm"
    className="flex-shrink-0"
  />
))}
```

Card sizes:
- `size="md"` (default): `w-20 md:w-24`, `h-28 md:h-36`
- `size="sm"`: `w-16`, `h-24`

## PersonImages Gallery

Photo gallery that reuses the `ImageGallery` component from media features:

```tsx
import { PersonImages } from "@/components/features/person";

{profileImages.length > 1 && (
  <PersonImages
    images={profileImages}
    personName={person.name}
    className="mt-8"
  />
)}
```

Features (inherited from ImageGallery):
- Horizontal scroll thumbnails with proper aspect ratio handling
- Click to open full-screen lightbox
- Keyboard navigation (←/→, Esc)
- Thumbnail strip at bottom of lightbox
- "+N more" button when images exceed maxVisible

## KnownForSection

Shows top credits by popularity with character names:

```tsx
import { KnownForSection } from "@/components/features/person";

<KnownForSection
  credits={person.combined_credits.cast}
  className="mt-8"
/>
```

Features:
- Filters out talk shows/news before sorting
- Shows character name as subtitle on each card
- Sorted by popularity, limited to top 12
- Uses MediaCard (respects card display preference)

## Credit to ListItem Conversion

When using `MovieCard` with person credits, convert to list item format:

```tsx
function creditToListItem(credit: PersonCombinedCastCredit): MovieListItem | SeriesListItem {
  if (credit.media_type === "movie") {
    return {
      id: credit.id,
      title: credit.title || "",
      poster_path: credit.poster_path,
      backdrop_path: credit.backdrop_path,
      vote_average: credit.vote_average,
      vote_count: credit.vote_count,
      release_date: credit.release_date || "",
      genre_ids: credit.genre_ids,
      overview: credit.overview,
      popularity: credit.popularity,
      adult: credit.adult,
      media_type: "movie",
    };
  }
  // Similar for TV...
}
```

## Person Card in Episode Modal

Guest Stars and Crew use squircle poster cards (`aspect-[2/3] rounded-lg`) matching the main cast scroller:

```tsx
function PersonCard({ person, role }) {
  return (
    <Link href={`/person/${person.id}`} className="flex-shrink-0 group">
      <div className="w-[85px] text-center">
        {/* Squircle poster aspect ratio */}
        <div className="relative aspect-[2/3] rounded-lg overflow-hidden bg-muted mb-1.5 ring-1 ring-white/10">
          {person.profile_path ? (
            <Image src={`https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185${person.profile_path}`} fill className="object-cover" />
          ) : (
            <User className="h-6 w-6 text-muted-foreground/30 absolute inset-0 m-auto" />
          )}
        </div>
        <p className="text-xs font-medium line-clamp-1">{person.name}</p>
        <p className="text-[10px] text-muted-foreground line-clamp-1">{person.character || person.job}</p>
      </div>
    </Link>
  );
}
```

**Person Scrollers use ScrollContainer:**
```tsx
<ScrollContainer showControls gap="gap-3" padding="px-0">
  {guestStars.map((guest) => (
    <PersonCard key={guest.id} person={guest} role="cast" />
  ))}
</ScrollContainer>
```
